WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.330
Bill Skarsgard's Pennywise has fast become
one of horror's most striking villains with

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:10.260
his droopy lip, wall-eyed look and iconic
red and white make-up joining the rogues gallery

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.650
of horror icons such as Freddy Krueger and
Michael Myers.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.730
But there are some fascinating and terrifying
early designs for the evil clown that didn't

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.000
make the final cut.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.970
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing nine horrifying cancelled

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:28.770
Pennywise designs and transformations you
never got to see in IT Chapters One and Two.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.500
And if you'd like a chance to win an awesome
Pennywise Funko Pop, be sure to subscribe

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.460
and keep watching for more details.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.660
Before arriving at the final look for Bill
Skarsgard's Pennywise, director Andy Muschietti

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:44.520
made a sketch in 2015 of what he thought the
murderous clown should look like.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:49.170
That sketch formed the basis for a set of
concept art by Daniel Carrasco and although

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.890
some of the features of these early designs
such as Pennywise's red and white make-up

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:57.289
were kept, other parts were scrapped and instead
Muschietti opted to give the villain some

00:00:57.289 --> 00:01:02.860
more pronounced baby-faced features such as
big eyes and apple cheeks as he felt the contrast

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:06.869
of the character's child-like features and
his terrifying behaviour would make him all

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:08.079
the more disturbing.

00:01:08.079 --> 00:01:12.539
Although these early designs are very cool,
a young child would have likely run a mile

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:15.229
as soon as they set eyes on such a clown.

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:19.579
Skarsgard's Pennywise with his cherub-like
cheeks, thick lips and more carefully manicured

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:24.779
hair is less immediately haunting in its appearance,
which is part of what helps it lure children

00:01:24.779 --> 00:01:27.490
into its gruesome traps.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:31.869
Watching Pennywise transform into a giant
spider-clown was pretty awesome in Chapter

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:32.869
Two.

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:36.600
And the final design was a vast improvement
on the spider form that IT took on at the

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.539
end of the 90s miniseries; though obviously,
there's a difference in budget between the

00:01:40.539 --> 00:01:44.810
TV show and films and the technology's advanced
massively since then.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:48.849
Still, part of the terrifying realism of the
spider-clown comes from the fact that Bill

00:01:48.849 --> 00:01:53.849
Skarsgard filmed these scenes in a motion-capture
suit so that the CGI monster retained many

00:01:53.849 --> 00:01:55.109
of the actor's facial features.

00:01:55.109 --> 00:02:00.430
And although it was pretty freaky seeing Pennywise's
head and torso attached to giant sharpened

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:05.159
spider-legs, early concept art revealed in
The World of IT book shows a different design

00:02:05.159 --> 00:02:10.819
that also gave the hybrid monster some disturbingly-long
human-like arms that had fingers not just

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:15.709
on the hands, but running all the way up the
arm, giving it a kind of caterpillar-style

00:02:15.709 --> 00:02:16.709
look.

00:02:16.709 --> 00:02:20.709
In this design, it seems like IT was grabbing
either Richie or Eddie in a similar way the

00:02:20.709 --> 00:02:24.099
IT spider did to Eddie in the TV series.

00:02:24.099 --> 00:02:28.709
We've seen Pennywise transform himself into
some pretty gross beings to terrorise the

00:02:28.709 --> 00:02:33.700
Losers such as the rotting, diseased Leper
that attacked Eddie outside the Neibolt House.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.769
However, an unused design for the spider-clown
gave Pennywise a rather vicious set of teeth

00:02:38.769 --> 00:02:44.069
on his derriere in what the concept designer
Vincent Proce called the Pennywise Arse Mouth.

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:48.659
The way this worked is that the upper parts
of each of Pennywise's main four spider-legs

00:02:48.659 --> 00:02:53.530
had hidden jaws with grinding teeth that when
put together formed what was effectively a

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:56.000
lethal mouth in the creature's butt.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:01.049
Then when Pennywise trapped a victim below
him, the jaws would open up to attack.

00:03:01.049 --> 00:03:04.280
Just imagine if we'd seen that in the final
film, it would probably have spawned a whole

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:09.150
series of memes to rival Pennywise the Dancing
Clown!

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:14.599
Watching the once powerful spider-clown Pennywise
shrink into a melted baby version of himself

00:03:14.599 --> 00:03:18.750
during his death scene was quite a sight to
behold and reminded me in some ways of an

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.319
infant Benjamin Button!

00:03:20.319 --> 00:03:24.489
But before the filmmakers arrived at the final
look for Pennywise during his last moments

00:03:24.489 --> 00:03:29.659
on earth, they toyed with other options including
a many-eyed version of the shrunken baby-clown.

00:03:29.659 --> 00:03:34.560
Yes, after the Losers had beaten down the
evil clown with the power of belief and insults,

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.769
there was almost going to be a version where
we would have seen baby Pennywise's still

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:42.150
over-sized head covered in a grotesque mass
of eyes.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:46.650
The inspiration behind all those eyes on the
spider-clown could be the fact that real-life

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.709
spiders have multiple eyes.

00:03:48.709 --> 00:03:52.650
Or perhaps it's a nod to the various many-eyed
beings in mythology and fiction.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:57.670
Either way, a multi-eyed and shrivelled Pennywise
would certainly have been the kind of freaky,

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:01.379
disgusting creature you wouldn't have been
able to stop looking at!

00:04:01.379 --> 00:04:05.900
And it might have been even creepier if those
many eyes also had Pennywise's signature creepy

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:10.409
wall-eyed look, shifting some of them in opposite
directions to the others.

00:04:10.409 --> 00:04:14.560
There's also some more concept art in the
World of IT book of regular Pennywise with

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.989
extra eyes in his forehead and also running
along the sides of his jaws when he opens

00:04:18.989 --> 00:04:20.739
them to reveal the deadlights.

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:24.360
And that too is truly the stuff of nightmares!

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.910
Another very creepy unused design for the
final Pennywise spider had the clown's head

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.870
wedged in the stomach of a big body.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.389
Above the clown's head was a disturbing skull
with outstretched arms.

00:04:35.389 --> 00:04:40.639
Then rather than well-defined spider-legs,
this monster had a mass of tentacle-like appendages

00:04:40.639 --> 00:04:41.639
below.

00:04:41.639 --> 00:04:45.080
And there's another surreal creature design
with tentacles as well as claws which give

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.460
it the feel of some kind of gross underwater-hybrid
monster.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:51.440
And one of the tentacles even has teeth and
eyes on it!

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.580
There's something of a baby-like quality to
these designs as well, which makes me think

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:59.990
of the awesomely horrific baby bug creature
that emerges from one of the fortune cookies

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:02.879
to terrify the Losers at the Chinese restaurant.

00:05:02.879 --> 00:05:06.940
And is a reminder that they've never been
able to have babies themselves and have to

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:11.930
retain child-like beliefs in order to defeat
IT once and for all.

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:16.270
Another set of unused Pennywise spider designs
seem to tip their hat to the spider version

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.319
of IT from the TV miniseries.

00:05:18.319 --> 00:05:22.220
The body is thicker on these designs than
the final version in the film, and this particular

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:27.490
shot of the spider raised up on its legs exposing
its abdomen reminds me of how the TV spider

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:30.660
revealed the deadlights to the Losers in the
final showdown.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:34.350
That was also the monster's weak spot and
the place where the Losers pulled out IT's

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.710
beating heart to defeat the evil entity in
the miniseries.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:43.129
A weirdly mesmerising transformation for Pennywise
that Andy Muschietti wanted to include was

00:05:43.129 --> 00:05:45.080
called "The Concentric Nightmare".

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:49.479
In The World of IT book, Muschietti describes
this unsettling look as "like a sock being

00:05:49.479 --> 00:05:51.150
turned inside out."

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:54.930
Accompanying the director's sketch of this
Pennywise monster are additional faces and

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:58.150
eyes that the monster's head would seem to
transform into.

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:03.470
According to Muschietti, the "Concentric Nightmare"
did appear ever so briefly in Chapter Two,

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:07.430
just after Eddie throws the spike Beverly
gave him through Pennywise's mouth to stop

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.289
it from deadlighting Richie.

00:06:09.289 --> 00:06:13.900
When the spike sticks in Pennywise's throat,
a version of the "Concentric Nightmare" appears

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:18.250
in a blink-and-you'll-miss-it moment before
Pennywise falls backwards and is stabbed.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:21.970
It's likely that this particular Pennywise
design was virtually scrapped in the end because

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:26.400
they wanted to go with more instantly recognisable
versions of IT that called back to previous

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.520
incarnations of the character we'd seen throughout
the movies.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:34.669
Also perhaps the concentric design was a little
too complex to work effectively in the fast-paced,

00:06:34.669 --> 00:06:36.639
strobe-lit finale.

00:06:36.639 --> 00:06:41.060
Mrs Kersh's transformation into the giant
witch that terrorises Beverly back at her

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.409
old home happens off-screen.

00:06:42.409 --> 00:06:48.370
But in early concept art, the plan was that
Bev would see the old lady turn into the many-mouthed

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:50.090
Pennywise monster in front of her eyes.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:53.860
Some of these early designs for the witch
look even more terrifying than the one that

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:54.860
ended up on screen.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:58.770
But I can see why they cut the character's
transformation scene as it makes the witch's

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.210
sudden appearance even more of a shock.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:05.360
There's an intriguing early human version
of Pennywise that was actually filmed and

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.550
shown in test screenings for Chapter One.

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:12.009
The scene wasn't included in either of the
theatrical releases for Chapters One or Two,

00:07:12.009 --> 00:07:16.009
but we do have a glimpse of what looks like
Pennywise's early human appearance in this

00:07:16.009 --> 00:07:17.009
photo.

00:07:17.009 --> 00:07:21.040
The scene, which was set in the 1600s, had
Pennywise terrorising a mother into giving

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:25.490
up her baby for him to eat and is an early
indicator of how It corrupted the inhabitants

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:28.310
of Derry to turn a blind eye to his evil.

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:32.500
The scene may actually show up in the six-hour
Supercut of both movies that Andy Muschietti

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:36.720
is planning and if you want to know all about
that and the other deleted scenes from Chapter

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.599
Two, tap here for my full deleted scenes video.

